      },
      "worked": "Choose four players in $\\binom{13}{4}$ ways. Choose one pair in $\\binom{4}{2}$ ways; the other pair is then fixed. Divide by $2$ because interchanging the teams counts the same match twice.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\binom{13}{4}\\times\\frac{\\binom{4}{2}}{2}\\\\N&=715\\times\\frac{6}{2}\\\\N&=2145.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
